# PowerShell scripts are checked out CRLF on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true stores LF in the index while working copies
# may hold either ending. Two files can then differ on disk while `git diff`
# reports nothing, because the index bytes are identical. That happened during
# the live-test harness work: live-test-db.ps1 sat LF on disk while its twin
# live-test-udt.ps1 was CRLF, and a byte-identity check between them went red
# for a difference no committed content contained.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
